# rsync --exclude-from list for deploys to the Apache docroot.
#
# Enumerated deliberately. A blanket dotfile pattern (.*) would match
# .htaccess, which is the site's ONLY rewrite configuration. Because the
# deploy runs with --delete, excluding it would silently strip it from the
# live site. Never add .htaccess to the pattern list below.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.deployignore
.htmlvalidate.json
.DS_Store
.superpowers/
docs/
scripts/
CLAUDE.md

# --- Server-managed paths ---
#
# Everything below protects files that live on the SERVER and are not part of
# this repo at all. rsync --delete only deletes receiver-side files that
# match a source-side path it is otherwise mirroring; a path excluded here is
# never considered for deletion, even though the repo has no corresponding
# file. Without these entries, a shared host's cgi-bin, its Let's Encrypt
# ACME challenge directory, log files, and htpasswd files would be wiped out
# by the next deploy. If your host manages other paths in the docroot
# (stats directories, mail webmail links, host-specific config), add them
# here too.
cgi-bin/
.well-known/
error_log
.htpasswd
